{{Term/Store|Amber|Ambers|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
Ambers are [[Material]]s that can be found in various [[Treasure Chest]]s. The [[Gem]]s can also often be found inside broken [[Ore Deposit]]s, and they sometimes appear inside [[Snowball]]s when they shatter. [[Stone Talus]]es and [[Stone Pebblit]] occasionally drop them as well. They are sold by [[Kairo]], who travels between [[Foothill Stable]] and the [[Maw of Death Mountain]]. 10 pieces of Amber can be used at [[Starlight Memories]] to create the [[Amber Earrings]], which use the Amber to harness the power of the land and increase defense.<ref name="BotW Inventory 2"/> The [[Kochi Dye Shop]] accepts Ambers as an ingredient to make [[Orange Dye]].

When speaking to [[Ramella]] in [[Goron City]], she will explain that if [[Link]] brings her 10 Ambers, she will pay more for them than a store will.<ref name="BotW Ramella"/> This will begin the [[Side Quest]] "[[The Jewel Trade]]". Afterwards, Link may sell batches of 10 Gems to Ramella in exchange for an increased payment.<ref name="BotW Ramella 2"/>

Ambers are required to [[Enhancing|Enhance]] the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|BotW|Amber}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
Ambers return as [[Material]]s in {{TotK}}. They are much sharper than they appeared in {{BotW}}.

Ambers are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]]:
{{Material Armors|TotK|Amber}}

==Other Appearances==
==={{AoC|-}}===
{{Noncanon|Start}}
Ambers as they are depicted in {{BotW}} are featured in {{AoC}}. They can be earned from [[Treasure Chest]]s or as a reward for completing [[Scenario]]s and [[Challenge]]s. As [[Material]]s, they can be used to fulfill [[Quest]] requirements.
{{Noncanon|End}}

